  {
    "heading": "4.0 Policies and Products Available",
    "body_paragraphs": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "In this lesson, you review the main **NFIP** policy forms and the product rules that shape how flood coverage applies. You will see when a Dwelling Policy fits, when a General Property Policy is the better match, and when a condominium association must use an RCBAP. We also explain how the former Preferred Risk Policy approach now appears within current residential flood coverage."
      },
      {
        "type": "bullet_list",
        "items": [
          "how you match policy types to residential, commercial, and condominium risks",
          "key flood policy terms you will use when you quote, issue, service, or discuss claims",
