          "most property located in, on, or over water, including open boathouse-type structures",
          "recreational vehicles and self-propelled vehicles, except certain limited machines kept inside and used mainly for the described location or to assist handicapped persons",
          "land, lawns, trees, shrubs, crops, animals, money, securities, and valuable papers"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bullet_list",
        "items": [
          "underground structures and equipment such as wells and septic systems",
          "outside walks, decks, driveways, patios, fences, seawalls, docks, piers, and bridges",
          "aircraft, watercraft, pools, and most hot tubs or spas",
          "property barred under Coastal Barrier Resources rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "You should also note special limits for below-ground property. If more than 49 percent of a building’s actual cash value is below ground, the building and contents are generally not covered, unless a narrow energy-efficient construction exception applies."
      }
