        "content": "Property can become ineligible when a building violates state or local floodplain management laws or ordinances. If that happens, contents and personal property in the building are also not eligible. You should watch for a Section 1316 issue. Under the National Flood Insurance Act, a state may place a violating structure on a 1316 Property List. Coverage can return if they correct the violation and the declaration is withdrawn."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "heading": "2.4 Ineligible Risks",
    "body_paragraphs": [
      {
