        "content": "Some risks are outside NFIP eligibility even if they relate to property. You should recognize common examples, including boathouses, boat repair docks, boat storage over water, campers, tents, swimming pools, fuel pumps, storage tanks, open stadiums, and separate drive-in bank teller units. Other items may qualify only if they meet the program's building definition, such as certain greenhouses, pavilions, pole barns, or pumping stations. Travel trailers usually are not eligible unless they are permanently converted and meet community permit rules. Water treatment plants also must satisfy the above-ground value test."
