        "content": "**National Flood Insurance Program (NFIP)** coverage was created by Congress in 1968 and is administered by FEMA. As you study this lesson, you will see how the program combines federal oversight with private insurer participation through the Write Your Own program. You will also learn why community floodplain rules matter before a policy can be issued."
      },
      {
        "type": "bullet_list",
