        "content": "You should also recognize risks the NFIP does not insure. Common examples include boat repair docks, boathouses, fuel pumps, open stadiums, tents, swimming pools, and separate drive-in bank teller units. Travel trailers are also ineligible unless they are converted into permanent onsite buildings that meet community permit rules. Some items, such as greenhouses, pavilions, pole barns, pumping stations, and water treatment plants, may qualify only if they meet the NFIP building standards. When you review an application, you should confirm that the structure is a true eligible building, not just a property feature or unsupported risk."
