    "heading": "2.5 Coastal Barrier Resources System and Other Protected Areas",
    "body_paragraphs": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Federal law limits flood insurance in certain protected coastal areas. The Coastal Barrier Resources Act and later amendments were designed to discourage development in high-risk coastal zones, reduce federal spending, and protect sensitive natural areas. If property is located in a designated Coastal Barrier Resources System area or other protected area, federal financial assistance, including flood insurance, may be barred. Before you discuss coverage, you should check current FEMA resources and community information."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "heading": "2.6 Who Needs Flood Insurance?",
    "body_paragraphs": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "People do not always buy flood insurance voluntarily. Under federal law, individuals, businesses, and others buying, building, or improving property in special flood hazard areas may need flood insurance to receive certain federal assistance or federally related financing. You should also explain that disaster aid is not automatic. Many events never receive a Presidential disaster declaration, and available aid is often a loan that must be repaid, sometimes over many years. For many clients, insurance is the more dependable source of flood recovery funds."
