        "content": "You should also know that FEMA’s flood maps and zones guide underwriting, rating, and some lender purchase requirements. In practice, many policies are written through the Write Your Own program, where private insurers issue and service the Standard Flood Insurance Policy while the federal government keeps the underwriting risk. As you work with clients, you must follow current FEMA rules and any guidance from state insurance regulators."
