    "body_paragraphs": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "An **eligible building** for NFIP coverage must have at least two outside rigid walls, a fully secured roof, and a permanent site. It must resist flotation, collapse, and lateral movement. Usually, at least 51% of the building’s actual cash value, including attached machinery and equipment, must be above ground. A limited exception applies when a below-ground level is designed with earth insulation and still meets base flood elevation requirements."
      }
    ]
