        "content": "When you rate an NFIP policy, you follow a set process so the premium matches the property’s flood risk. Start with the exact property location. If the mailing address is different, you use the property address because the insured location drives the flood zone and rating. You also confirm that the building is in a participating community. If the community does not participate in the NFIP, flood coverage is not available through the program."
